Fillets and chamfers: 0073's pieces of an analytic blend that are one face,
on a spine closed by one edge (mitcad#263).

The case: a boss under a plate chamfered past the plate's rounded corner
(0142); the file has the chamfer's cone as one face, cut by the plate's
sides. 0073 joins a run of pieces that leaves the faces of a piece and
comes back to them, consecutive in the spine's parameters, on one surface.
On a closed spine:

- the piece across the spine's start holds its spine parameters a period
  on, so the run's pieces did not follow each other: the gap between them
  is now taken modulo the period;
- the run may go on across the spine's start, from the last pieces round
  to the first ones (the boss's seam in the gap): runs are followed round
  a spine closed by its one edge, and each joined piece takes the surface
  of the piece before it in its run, in the order of the run, with no
  run making a loop;
- the joined pieces' p-curves on the blend surface go on from the piece
  before's, in its period (ChFi3d_PCurvesOnSurfAfter), as one face needs.

Before, the cone of the case came in four or five faces.

